# Code owners for kerkit.
#
# kerkit is currently maintained by one person; every path resolves to the sole
# maintainer. When a second maintainer / recovery owner is added to the @kerkit
# npm org (see RELEASING.md "Access & recovery"), add them here so review and
# release ownership are shared in more than one place.
#
# GitHub requests review from these owners automatically. It does NOT enforce
# their approval unless the `main` ruleset / branch protection requires review
# from Code Owners — see the manual branch-protection step in RELEASING.md.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
*                        @JuanseHevia

# Launch, CI, and community-health surfaces.
/.github/                @JuanseHevia
/docs/                   @JuanseHevia
/SECURITY.md             @JuanseHevia
/SUPPORT.md              @JuanseHevia

# Release-critical surface (more specific — listed last so it takes precedence):
# publish workflow, release runbook, changeset config, scripts, and package
# manifests. Changes here can alter what/how we publish.
/.github/workflows/      @JuanseHevia
/.changeset/             @JuanseHevia
/RELEASING.md            @JuanseHevia
/scripts/                @JuanseHevia
/packages/*/package.json @JuanseHevia
